# diff-digital-device's rulings (tests/differential/comp.zig `readRulings`): where old
# `vera --check` of a .v is wrong. One line per fixture: `<path> <clause>: why`. A ruled
# fixture agrees only while its tiebreak holds (comp/device.zig): the fixture is no
# `//! reject`, the new side builds the device, and that device, written by
# `vera-next --emit-zig` and stepped by tests/host/vdev_run.zig, commits byte for byte
# the transcript `vera-next --run` prints.
verilog/03_lexical_conventions/ams_lexical_escaped_ascii.v VAMS-2023 §7.8 (a design with no ports is a device of no pins): the old device of a pinless top does not compile (lib/sim/rt/device.zig indexes an empty `spec.pins`), an engine bug by its own message
